block content
    h1 Indigestion
    p Definition by #[a(href="https://www.mayoclinic.org/diseases-conditions/indigestion/symptoms-causes/syc-20352211") Mayo Clinic]:
    blockquote Indigestion — also called dyspepsia or an upset stomach — is discomfort in your upper abdomen. Indigestion describes certain symptoms, such as belly pain and a feeling of fullness soon after you start eating, rather than a specific disease. Indigestion can also be a symptom of other digestive disorders.
